# Copy this file to your Umbrel at EXACTLY this name and location:
#   ~/umbrel/app-data/brandonjamesmarshall-transmission/.env
# It MUST be named ".env" (leading dot) and sit directly in the app folder
# — NOT in a data/ subfolder. gluetun and the seedbox-refresh sidecar read
# it via the env_file directive in docker-compose.yml. Do NOT commit real
# values.
#
# Generate a WireGuard keypair locally:
#   brew install wireguard-tools          # on Mac (or apt-get install -y wireguard-tools on Linux)
#   wg genkey | tee >(wg pubkey > pub.key) > priv.key
# Paste the PUBLIC key into your VPN provider's account area under WireGuard
# (e.g. iVPN: https://www.ivpn.net/account), and the provider will return
# your assigned tunnel address.

VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=custom
VPN_TYPE=wireguard

# Your 44-char base64 private key (the value of `cat priv.key`)
WIREGUARD_PRIVATE_KEY=replace-with-your-private-key

# The address your provider assigned (e.g. 172.28.135.212/32) — include the /32
WIREGUARD_ADDRESSES=replace-with-your-assigned-ip/32

# --- Pin ONE VPN server via a CUSTOM WireGuard endpoint ---
# Some private trackers require a SEMI-STABLE exit IP (changes less than
# once/hour); an unstable IP triggers "Unrecognized host/passkey" errors
# and can get tracker access auto-disabled. Stability comes from pinning
# ONE server.
#
# Pin with a CUSTOM endpoint (VPN_SERVICE_PROVIDER=custom, above) instead of
# a provider name + SERVER_HOSTNAMES/SERVER_CITIES filter. Using iVPN as the
# worked example throughout:
#   - SERVER_CITIES=Zurich ROTATES across iVPN's three Zurich servers, which
#     span two ASNs / three IP blocks (ch1=M247 185.212.170.x, ch2=Privatelayer
#     81.17.24.x, ch3=Privatelayer 141.255.166.x) — exactly the IP flapping
#     such trackers punish; and
#   - gluetun's BAKED-IN server list goes stale: iVPN re-IPs servers (it moved
#     ch1 from Privatelayer 141.255.x to M247 185.212.170.x in 2026), so a
#     pinned hostname can map to a DEAD endpoint and gluetun loops forever on
#     "healthcheck i/o timeout".
# A custom endpoint pins the live server IP + key directly, entirely in this
# .env — immune to gluetun's stale list, nothing written into umbrel app-data.
#
# EXAMPLE below = ch1.wg.ivpn.net (Zurich, M247) — swap in any server from
# YOUR provider's P2P-allowed list. The three values (ENDPOINT_IP,
# ENDPOINT_PORT, PUBLIC_KEY) describe ONE server: always replace all three
# together, taken from the SAME server — mixing one server's IP with
# another's key fails the handshake silently. Server endpoint values are
# PUBLIC and shared by all of a provider's users — only your two keys above
# (private key + assigned address) are yours. ENDPOINT_IP must be a literal
# IP; gluetun's custom mode does not resolve hostnames.
#
# TWO DIFFERENT IPs (this trips people up): WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP below
# (185.212.170.141) is the server's WireGuard LISTEN address that gluetun
# connects TO. Your EXIT IP — 185.212.170.142, the public IP trackers see,
# and the value that goes in a tracker seedbox session's "IP" field — is
# NAT'd behind it. They are SUPPOSED to differ; do NOT give a tracker the
# endpoint IP.
WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP=185.212.170.141
WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_PORT=2049
WIREGUARD_PUBLIC_KEY=dU7gLfcupYd37LW0q6cxC6PHMba+eUFAUOoU/ryXZkY=
#
# Failover — swap ALL THREE values above if ch1 is down/retired. Current Zurich
# servers (iVPN re-IPs/re-keys, so re-check before relying on these):
#   ch2.wg.ivpn.net  81.17.24.165     KRKeAFMJY6OH9RABaeC4feQG/JgbacZVg/w6VUjBSVQ=
#   ch3.wg.ivpn.net  141.255.166.198  JBpgBKtqIneRuEga7mbP2PAk/e4HPRaC11H0A0+R3lA=
# Re-fetch any server's live key, and dig its hostname for the current IP:
#   curl -fsS https://api.ivpn.net/v4/servers/stats \
#     | jq -r '.servers[]|select(.city=="Zurich")|"\(.hostnames.wireguard) \(.isp) \(.wg_public_key)"'
#   dig +short ch1.wg.ivpn.net        # -> WIREGUARD_ENDPOINT_IP
# iVPN P2P-allowed list:
# https://www.ivpn.net/knowledgebase/general/which-vpn-servers-can-i-use-for-p2p-torrent-traffic/

# Optional:
# LOG_LEVEL=debug
# DOT_PROVIDERS=cloudflare,quad9

# Note: Transmission's RPC username/password are set via the USER and PASS
# env vars in docker-compose.yml (default user "admin"; the password is the
# per-install value umbrelOS shows on the app card). Edit the compose to
# change them.

# --- Private tracker dynamic seedbox (optional) ---
# Some private trackers offer a "dynamic seedbox" API: an authenticated
# endpoint that (re)authorizes whatever source IP the call arrives from.
# The seedbox-refresh sidecar calls it from inside the VPN tunnel so your
# VPN exit IP stays authorized for seeding. It expects a JSON response
# containing "Success":true and respects the common 1-update-per-hour rate
# limit — mostly insurance now that the exit IP is pinned, but it covers
# NAT-pool shifts and future server re-IPs.
#
# On the tracker, create a DEDICATED session for this (usually under
# Preferences -> Security):
#   * IP-locked, NOT ASN-locked — VPN providers span multiple ASNs, so an
#     ASN-locked session rejects the update the moment your exit ASN changes
#   * dynamic-seedbox permission enabled
#   * initial IP = your VPN EXIT IP (e.g. 185.212.170.142), NOT your home IP
#   * label it (e.g. "umbrel transmission seedbox") so cleanup doesn't
#     confuse it with your indexer (Prowlarr) session — keep that one; it's
#     locked to your home connection and feeds the indexer
# Some trackers also want your VPN provider registered on your profile
# (a shared VPN exit IP can otherwise look like account sharing) — check
# yours and register the provider if so.
#
# SEEDBOX_UPDATE_URL = the tracker's dynamic-seedbox endpoint (full URL).
#                      Leave blank if you don't use one — the sidecar then
#                      idles (exit 0).
# SEEDBOX_COOKIE     = OPTIONAL: that session's cookie as name=value
#                      (exactly what curl -b expects). Only needed when the
#                      tracker authenticates the endpoint with a session
#                      cookie; leave blank if yours token-auths via the URL.
SEEDBOX_COOKIE=
SEEDBOX_UPDATE_URL=
